    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1700-a1">

                <pb facs="1446" n="1342" xml:id="pg1342"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure—Identic note verbale.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Embassy to the
                            Ministry for Foreign Affairs.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-02-22">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 22, 1913</hi>.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Embassy of the United States of America regrets being unable to agree with
                    the point of view expressed by the Imperial Ministry in its note verbale dated
                    January 30 last, on the subject of the requisition for war purposes of horses
                    and vehicles belonging to foreign subjects.</p>
                <p>The principal object of the communications which the Embassy has had the honor to
                    address to the Imperial Ministry on the question was to assure in these
                    proceedings, in so far as they concern its nationals and under the reserves
                    formulated, the guaranties of a general sort established by the treaties and by
                    custom.</p>
                <p>Every sort of requisition, as well as the appraisement for the purpose of
                    offering the interested party a fair compensation, can therefore take place only
                    with the presence of a consular delegate.</p>
                <p>It naturally remains understood that the payment for objects requisitioned should
                    be arranged at the very time of the requisition, either in money or by draft
                    accepted by the Imperial Ottoman Bank.</p>
            </div>
